{"name":"Individual White","hex":"#d4cdca","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"individual","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person considered alone, rather than as belonging to a group of people.","A single physical human being as a legal subject, as opposed to a legal person such as a corporation."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to a single person or thing as opposed to more than one.","Intended for a single person as opposed to more than one person."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/individual"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Individual","blocks":[{"text":"An individual is one that exists as a distinct entity. Individuality is the state or quality of living as an individual; particularly as a person unique from other people and possessing one's own needs or goals, rights and responsibilities. The concept of an individual features in many fields, including biology, law, and philosophy. Every individual contributes significantly to the growth of a civilization. Society is a multifaceted concept that is shaped and influenced by a wide range of different things, including human behaviors, attitudes, and ideas. The culture, morals, and beliefs of others as well as the general direction and trajectory of the society can all be influenced and shaped by an individual's activities."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Individual","wikidata":"Q795052"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Finnish_anti-vegetation_task_force_on_a_Baltic_sea_island.jpg/500px-Finnish_anti-vegetation_task_force_on_a_Baltic_sea_island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Finnish_anti-vegetation_task_force_on_a_Baltic_sea_island.jpg/1280px-Finnish_anti-vegetation_task_force_on_a_Baltic_sea_island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Finnish_anti-vegetation_task_force_on_a_Baltic_sea_island.jpg/500px-Finnish_anti-vegetation_task_force_on_a_Baltic_sea_island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Individuals may stand out from the crowd, or may blend in with it.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFinnish_anti-vegetation_task_force_on_a_Baltic_sea_island.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Free_To_Be_Me_artwork_piece_in_a_library_%282%29.jpg/500px-Free_To_Be_Me_artwork_piece_in_a_library_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Free_To_Be_Me_artwork_piece_in_a_library_%282%29.jpg/1280p